Hint:\(\nu={RcZ}^2\left(\frac{1}{{n}_1^2}-\frac{1}{{n}_2^2}\right) \)

Step: Find the series limit for the pfund series.
The frequency of the hydrogen transition is given by;
\(\nu={RcZ}^2\left(\frac{1}{{n}_1^2}-\frac{1}{{n}_2^2}\right) \)
For\(Z=1\), Lyman series (\(n_1 = 1, n_2 = \infty\)) the series limit frequency
is given by;
\(\nu_L={Rc}\left(\frac{1}{{1}^2}-\frac{1}{{\infty}^2}\right) ~~~...(1)\)
For\(Z=1\), pfund series (\(n_1 = 5, n_2 = \infty\)) the series limit frequency
is given by;
\(\nu_P={Rc}\left(\frac{1}{{5}^2}-\frac{1}{{\infty}^2}\right) ~~~...(2)\)
From equation \((1)\) and \((2)\) we get;
\(\nu_P = \dfrac{\nu_L}{25}\)
